\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The trading filter in the frequency domain, $|H(\omega )|\propto N(\omega )^{-1/2}$. (a)~Power-law impact ($\eta =\lambda =0$) gives a scale-free fractional filter of slope $-(1+\beta )/2$. (b)~The friction family ($\gamma =1$, $\kappa =2$, $\lambda =0.5$, and $\eta =0.3$ where present): inventory risk sets a low-frequency plateau, exponential transient impact a resilience shelf, temporary cost a high-frequency rolloff, and power-law impact a fractional tail, with crossover frequencies $\omega _c,\omega _*$.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
