\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Impact surfing. (a)~The flow response $R(\theta )$ for the exponential kernel ($\gamma =1$, $\kappa =2$) changes sign at $\theta ^*=\kappa -2m$ as inventory risk $\lambda $ grows; the power-law kernel never flips. (b)~Phase diagram in $(\theta ,\lambda )$: the optimum follows the signal ($R>0$) below $\theta ^*(\lambda )$ and surfs its own transient impact ($R<0$) above, surfing at every signal speed once $\lambda \ge 2\kappa \gamma /3$.}}{14}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:surf}{{8}{14}{Impact surfing. (a)~The flow response $R(\theta )$ for the exponential kernel ($\gamma =1$, $\kappa =2$) changes sign at $\theta ^*=\kappa -2m$ as inventory risk $\lambda $ grows; the power-law kernel never flips. (b)~Phase diagram in $(\theta ,\lambda )$: the optimum follows the signal ($R>0$) below $\theta ^*(\lambda )$ and surfs its own transient impact ($R<0$) above, surfing at every signal speed once $\lambda \ge 2\kappa \gamma /3$}{figure.8}{}}
